  "id": "COMPOUND:7843 - PROTEIN:1108",
  "verbalization": "Arbaclofen is implicated in the regulation of RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase through a multi-step pathway involving interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha and trans-Norbixin. The evidence suggests that Arbaclofen acts as a target for interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha, which in turn is a target of trans-Norbixin, both of which ultimately target RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase. This indicates a potential mechanism where Arbaclofen may influence the signaling pathways through these intermediaries, possibly by modulating receptor activity or downstream signaling cascades. The presence of multiple indirect pathways linking Arbaclofen to RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase highlights the complexity of the relationship, but the consistent involvement of interleukin-11 receptor subunit alpha and trans-Norbixin as intermediaries supports a plausible mechanism. The integration of these pathways suggests that Arbaclofen may exert its effects through a network of targets that ultimately converge on RAF proto-oncogene serine/threonine-protein kinase, potentially through the modulation of receptor signaling or other cellular processes.",
